  "description": "The Nerd JR is the ultimate kid’s mountain bike. With 120mm travel front and rear, 24” wheels, and the option to upgrade to 26”, the Nerd will last for years and handle any kind of riding. Great effort has gone into dialing this bike. This is not just another addition to the range like many kid's bikes - we took this project very seriously. Our goal was to make it capable of growing with the child and making it suitable for various types of mountain bike riding - anything from XC to freeride. One of the key features is the possibility to upgrade the bike to 26” when the time comes. After the wheel swap the bike still retains correct geometry. Developed and tested by the NS Bikes founder and his son, this is really a dream kid’s bike.\nINTENDED USE CATEGORY 6: ALL MOUNTAIN\nMAIN FEATURES:\n-light alloy frame with yoke driven shock\n- tough double pass welds\n- sold with 24” wheels but will accept 26”\n- 120mm front / 120mm rear wheel travel\n- air shock and fork work properly under kid's weight\n- Light and reliable wheels build on sealed bearing hubs\n- Shimano 10spd derailleur\nSHOCK IS ACTUATED BY AN ELEGANT FORGED YOKE KINEMATICS OPTIMIZED FOR AN AGGRESSIVE RIDING. LATERALY STABLE REAR TRIANGLE HELD BY THREE OVERSIZED MAX BEARIGS\nORIGINAL 24\" WHEELS ARE OPTIMAL FOR 6-8 OLD KIDS (125-135CM)\nTALLER KIDS CAN SWITCH TO 26” AND AT THE SAME TIME",
